  "id": "Compound::DB01118 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Amiodarone is linked to Cyp2d6 through a series of molecular interactions that involve different compounds. The evidence suggests that Amiodarone causes Neuromyopathy, which is associated with Chloroquine or Hydroxychloroquine, both of which bind to Cyp2d6. Praziquantel, another compound linked to Amiodarone, also binds to Cyp2d6. This indicates that Amiodarone may influence Cyp2d6 through the metabolic pathways of these compounds. The lowest common ancestor of these relationships is the Organooxygen Compound or Oxygen Molecular Entity, suggesting a broader metabolic or enzymatic context. The evidence supports a mechanism where Amiodarone indirectly affects Cyp2d6 via the metabolic activation of related compounds, highlighting a potential dependency on these pathways. The integration of these findings suggests that Amiodarone may modulate Cyp2d6 activity through the metabolic activation of other substances, emphasizing the role of these compounds in the drug's pharmacological effects.",
